    "body": "Thanks for the report, I can confirm this is what happens (mainline, version .30dev).\r\n\r\nThere's two things going on here.\r\n1. There is a problem in that creating an array with a `dtype` specified by string doesn't work yet, https://github.com/numba/numba/issues/2201.\r\n2. Numba should have reported that opposed to giving the error you report.\r\n\r\nThankfully, as a user end fix, if the `dtype` to `cuda.local.array` is specified like:\r\n```\r\nfrom numba import float64\r\n...\r\n...\r\ndef kern(arr)\r\n    toarr=cuda.local.array(10, float64)\r\n```\r\nthen your code should compile.\r\n\r\n",
